When you’re managing 10, 50, 100+ applications, the default ArgoCD setup won’t cut it.

That’s where the App of Apps Pattern shines. Here’s why 👇

🏗️ What is it?
Instead of manually creating dozens of ArgoCD Application CRDs, you create a single parent app — which declares all other apps.

It’s GitOps composability at its best.

💡 Benefits:
 • ✅ Centralized bootstrapping
 • ✅ Modular structure per team/service
 • ✅ Clean Git repo org (e.g. one folder per app)
 • ✅ Easier RBAC + multi-tenant management
 • ✅ Clean separation of concerns

🧱 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼 𝗦𝘁𝗿𝘂𝗰𝘁𝘂𝗿𝗲 𝗘𝘅𝗮𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗲:

    apps/
    ├── team-a/
    │  ├── frontend/
    │  └── backend/
    ├── team-b/
     │  └── analytics/
    root-app.yaml → includes all above apps

🛠️ Tips:
Use 𝘒𝘶𝘴𝘵𝘰𝘮𝘪𝘻𝘦 or 𝘏𝘦𝘭𝘮 to compose apps

Separate environments using overlays (dev/, prod/)

Use sync waves to control app rollout order

📌 TL;DR
One Git repo. One root app.
Dozens of services. Scalable and clean.
